><italic>Echinococcus granulosus</italic>: DNA extraction from germinal layers allows strain determination in fertile and nonfertile hydatid cysts.</article-title><source>Exp Parasitol</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>122</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10910713</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000426-Lahmar1"><label>5</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lahmar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Debbek</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name><name><surname>McManus</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Souissi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Transmission dynamics of the <italic>Echinococcus granulosus</italic> sheep-dog strain (G1 genotype) in camels in Tunisia.</article-title><source>Vet Parasitol</source><volume>121</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15110412</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000426-Craig1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Qiu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Echinococcosis and Tibetan communities.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source><volume>14</volume><fpage>1674</fpage><lpage>1675</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18826849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000426-Heath1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heath</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><sur